[{:db/id 17592186096707 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-48d7d71f-4c73-5bda-b5f4-b80929ee461c" "question-d5da328f-bab5-5074-ba79-45d8e6dffb79" "question-af6bef8d-9bda-5865-8318-f03b8c8ed1c7" "question-906c2725-0c67-5b11-96ab-a36547c9a017"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096706 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-165f408f-fdbf-512c-a0a1-ee39f4be587e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096708 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a25c3b40-7f3b-57d8-a341-b7f66aac34c1" "question-4260057c-f969-5185-9095-04c56e87e760" "question-baa62b58-d974-5e44-ba9b-341e234529fa"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-48d7d71f-4c73-5bda-b5f4-b80929ee461c" :question/id #uuid "48d7d71f-4c73-5bda-b5f4-b80929ee461c" :question/math-academy-id "q-251439" :question/problem "**From top to bottom**, the points of intersection of the parabola ${y}^{2}-12x-2y-8=0$ with the $y$-axis are $A$ and $B.$ Find the coordinates of $A$ and $B.$\n\n$A(${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)\\,$ and $\\,B(${{field-3}}$,$\n{{field-4}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "When the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we set $x=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-12(0)-2y-8 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-2y-8 & =0 \\\\ (y+2)(y-4) & =0 \\\\ y & =-2,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the intersection points, from top to bottom, are $(0,4)$ and $(0,-2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dbfacd55-1c0e-5862-bb80-6a63da7af696" "answer-field-435eda17-3222-5b4f-814b-e869d3ae12c3" "answer-field-27782995-11b2-5ae4-9e09-6f5e83391567" "answer-field-1be16104-19f9-514e-9edd-dc5c316b5114"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dbfacd55-1c0e-5862-bb80-6a63da7af696" :answer-field/id #uuid "dbfacd55-1c0e-5862-bb80-6a63da7af696" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-59d1c638-bc43-5894-9c3f-b999d8f59e6d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-59d1c638-bc43-5894-9c3f-b999d8f59e6d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59d1c638-bc43-5894-9c3f-b999d8f59e6d" :answer/id #uuid "59d1c638-bc43-5894-9c3f-b999d8f59e6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-435eda17-3222-5b4f-814b-e869d3ae12c3" :answer-field/id #uuid "435eda17-3222-5b4f-814b-e869d3ae12c3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8056f24c-ed86-5bbd-af9e-159b07e24646" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8056f24c-ed86-5bbd-af9e-159b07e24646"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8056f24c-ed86-5bbd-af9e-159b07e24646" :answer/id #uuid "8056f24c-ed86-5bbd-af9e-159b07e24646" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-27782995-11b2-5ae4-9e09-6f5e83391567" :answer-field/id #uuid "27782995-11b2-5ae4-9e09-6f5e83391567" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-557f7731-a814-5f95-8ddd-ff3a6a627548" :answer-field/choices ["answer-557f7731-a814-5f95-8ddd-ff3a6a627548"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-557f7731-a814-5f95-8ddd-ff3a6a627548" :answer/id #uuid "557f7731-a814-5f95-8ddd-ff3a6a627548" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1be16104-19f9-514e-9edd-dc5c316b5114" :answer-field/id #uuid "1be16104-19f9-514e-9edd-dc5c316b5114" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-15ab6d36-955b-5319-b4c2-4ceabe2971b7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-15ab6d36-955b-5319-b4c2-4ceabe2971b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15ab6d36-955b-5319-b4c2-4ceabe2971b7" :answer/id #uuid "15ab6d36-955b-5319-b4c2-4ceabe2971b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d5da328f-bab5-5074-ba79-45d8e6dffb79" :question/id #uuid "d5da328f-bab5-5074-ba79-45d8e6dffb79" :question/math-academy-id "q-14280" :question/problem "Find the points of intersection of the parabola ${y}^{2}=-8(x-16)$ with the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "When the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we set $x=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =-8(0-16) \\\\ {y}^{2} & =128 \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{128} \\\\ y & =\\pm 8\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola intersects the $y$-axis at $(0,8\\sqrt{2})$ and $(0,-8\\sqrt{2}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f11adb4f-a6df-5572-a829-d227a29ca6f0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f11adb4f-a6df-5572-a829-d227a29ca6f0" :answer-field/id #uuid "f11adb4f-a6df-5572-a829-d227a29ca6f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-05b4bc6f-6eae-58f3-bd4e-a6df1a6e19f7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c47ad941-a4b2-5c3c-af7a-07dadfbe2daa" "answer-7ea9ba4a-4b8b-5bad-a45e-00c2f7caa19d" "answer-05b4bc6f-6eae-58f3-bd4e-a6df1a6e19f7" "answer-75638e1e-4fe2-5380-80d6-466225c94b00" "answer-549b8f34-438a-55fd-81c8-cc57361533ee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c47ad941-a4b2-5c3c-af7a-07dadfbe2daa" :answer/id #uuid "c47ad941-a4b2-5c3c-af7a-07dadfbe2daa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,4\\sqrt{3})$ and $(0,-4\\sqrt{3})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ea9ba4a-4b8b-5bad-a45e-00c2f7caa19d" :answer/id #uuid "7ea9ba4a-4b8b-5bad-a45e-00c2f7caa19d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,4\\sqrt{7})$ and $(0,-4\\sqrt{7})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05b4bc6f-6eae-58f3-bd4e-a6df1a6e19f7" :answer/id #uuid "05b4bc6f-6eae-58f3-bd4e-a6df1a6e19f7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,8\\sqrt{2})$ and $(0,-8\\sqrt{2})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75638e1e-4fe2-5380-80d6-466225c94b00" :answer/id #uuid "75638e1e-4fe2-5380-80d6-466225c94b00" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,8\\sqrt{5})$ and $(0,-8\\sqrt{5})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-549b8f34-438a-55fd-81c8-cc57361533ee" :answer/id #uuid "549b8f34-438a-55fd-81c8-cc57361533ee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(8\\sqrt{3},0)$ and $(-8\\sqrt{3},0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-af6bef8d-9bda-5865-8318-f03b8c8ed1c7" :question/id #uuid "af6bef8d-9bda-5865-8318-f03b8c8ed1c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-251434" :question/problem "The parabola ${y}^{2}-3x+12y+36=0$ intersects the $x$-axis at the point$\\,(${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$).$" :question/worked-solution "When the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we set $y=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-3x+12y+36 & =0 \\\\ (0)^{2}-3x+12(0)+36 & =0 \\\\ -3x+36 & =0 \\\\ -3x & =-36 \\\\ x & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola intersects the $x$-axis at $(12,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9f4b1bc8-53fc-58ca-a338-90cc2e17cebf" "answer-field-b7e72b22-0ede-5974-9f47-a89f67fcf4d2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9f4b1bc8-53fc-58ca-a338-90cc2e17cebf" :answer-field/id #uuid "9f4b1bc8-53fc-58ca-a338-90cc2e17cebf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6ec967a6-45c9-582d-b788-eca41cd0c25a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6ec967a6-45c9-582d-b788-eca41cd0c25a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ec967a6-45c9-582d-b788-eca41cd0c25a" :answer/id #uuid "6ec967a6-45c9-582d-b788-eca41cd0c25a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b7e72b22-0ede-5974-9f47-a89f67fcf4d2" :answer-field/id #uuid "b7e72b22-0ede-5974-9f47-a89f67fcf4d2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0153ff6d-d05a-56ce-9b58-02c01757d0ac" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0153ff6d-d05a-56ce-9b58-02c01757d0ac"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0153ff6d-d05a-56ce-9b58-02c01757d0ac" :answer/id #uuid "0153ff6d-d05a-56ce-9b58-02c01757d0ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-906c2725-0c67-5b11-96ab-a36547c9a017" :question/id #uuid "906c2725-0c67-5b11-96ab-a36547c9a017" :question/math-academy-id "q-73764" :question/problem "Find the point of intersection of the parabola\n$(y-9)^{2}=-3x$\nwith the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "When the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we set $y=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-9)^{2} & =-3x \\\\ 81 & =-3x \\\\ x & =-27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola intersects the $x$-axis at $(-27,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-58b63720-0427-5c5f-80b8-922ecf25b780"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-58b63720-0427-5c5f-80b8-922ecf25b780" :answer-field/id #uuid "58b63720-0427-5c5f-80b8-922ecf25b780" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-161002e7-3475-55d1-bf33-13e031fadd4a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-161002e7-3475-55d1-bf33-13e031fadd4a" "answer-ace6d14a-2a71-536b-8bbd-cd9914aff9ed" "answer-4134ea6b-accb-5265-8339-c07c21944ba0" "answer-a5b77d34-ec2b-5142-964b-faad40063dd1" "answer-ddf67998-b0d8-57b1-bbac-1c4711ac29d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-161002e7-3475-55d1-bf33-13e031fadd4a" :answer/id #uuid "161002e7-3475-55d1-bf33-13e031fadd4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-27,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ace6d14a-2a71-536b-8bbd-cd9914aff9ed" :answer/id #uuid "ace6d14a-2a71-536b-8bbd-cd9914aff9ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-9,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4134ea6b-accb-5265-8339-c07c21944ba0" :answer/id #uuid "4134ea6b-accb-5265-8339-c07c21944ba0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,27)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5b77d34-ec2b-5142-964b-faad40063dd1" :answer/id #uuid "a5b77d34-ec2b-5142-964b-faad40063dd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(27,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ddf67998-b0d8-57b1-bbac-1c4711ac29d3" :answer/id #uuid "ddf67998-b0d8-57b1-bbac-1c4711ac29d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-165f408f-fdbf-512c-a0a1-ee39f4be587e" :question/id #uuid "165f408f-fdbf-512c-a0a1-ee39f4be587e" :question/math-academy-id "q-165432" :question/problem "![](images/db/dbf4056d9e2709bd959f4b8b79168941247af16ed1ae1b5dceb716cabe424830.png)\n\nWhat are the $x$-intercepts of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(3,4)$ and passes through the point $(2,3).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(3,4)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2} & =4p(y-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(2,3),$ we substitute $x=2$ and $y=3$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2-3)^{2} & =4p(3-4) \\\\ 1 & =4p(-1) \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2} & =-(y-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2} & =-(0-4) \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{4} \\\\ x & =\\pm 2+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts are $1$ and $5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-95e16fd0-a1f9-576d-8004-2a0b51672b20"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-95e16fd0-a1f9-576d-8004-2a0b51672b20" :answer-field/id #uuid "95e16fd0-a1f9-576d-8004-2a0b51672b20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d6831979-452b-5430-b4b7-e4fc46bb3bee" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cb0b6c80-8dbc-56a7-a1a0-d14593c8129b" "answer-23b9a138-ccef-5b44-bdde-523564d8cad9" "answer-3e9d1839-ab38-5603-9316-98bd943923cc" "answer-d6831979-452b-5430-b4b7-e4fc46bb3bee" "answer-26111051-d566-5d79-af8c-be170c78e32b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb0b6c80-8dbc-56a7-a1a0-d14593c8129b" :answer/id #uuid "cb0b6c80-8dbc-56a7-a1a0-d14593c8129b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\sqrt{3}+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23b9a138-ccef-5b44-bdde-523564d8cad9" :answer/id #uuid "23b9a138-ccef-5b44-bdde-523564d8cad9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\sqrt{5}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e9d1839-ab38-5603-9316-98bd943923cc" :answer/id #uuid "3e9d1839-ab38-5603-9316-98bd943923cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\sqrt{5}+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6831979-452b-5430-b4b7-e4fc46bb3bee" :answer/id #uuid "d6831979-452b-5430-b4b7-e4fc46bb3bee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$ and $5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26111051-d566-5d79-af8c-be170c78e32b" :answer/id #uuid "26111051-d566-5d79-af8c-be170c78e32b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{3}{2}$ and $\\frac{21}{4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a25c3b40-7f3b-57d8-a341-b7f66aac34c1" :question/id #uuid "a25c3b40-7f3b-57d8-a341-b7f66aac34c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-251826" :question/problem "![](images/0e/0e95f9087b5b607f2d33d49c0f5db123eede589e53adc94747f3a33c1fe68f90.png)\n\n**From top to bottom**, the **exact** values of the $y$-intercepts of the parabola shown above are{{field-1}}\nand \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-8,-1)$ and passes through the point $(-6,1).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola with vertex at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),\n$$\n\nand substituting $(h,k)=(-8,-1)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(y+1)^{2}=4p(x+8).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(-6,1),$ we substitute $x=-6$ and $y=1$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1+1)^{2} & =4p(-6+8) \\\\ 4 & =4p(2) \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =2(x+8).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =2(0+8) \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =16 \\\\ y+1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{16} \\\\ y & =\\pm 4-1 \\\\ y & =-5,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from top to bottom, the $y$-intercepts are $3$ and  $-5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-91e3b777-9db3-51a5-ab92-8bddd54cd065" "answer-field-78edd9c5-7539-5d54-8eb1-437fb325e3d3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-91e3b777-9db3-51a5-ab92-8bddd54cd065" :answer-field/id #uuid "91e3b777-9db3-51a5-ab92-8bddd54cd065" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c1fd71a3-f959-5632-b94a-c770e9c6d2a3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c1fd71a3-f959-5632-b94a-c770e9c6d2a3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c1fd71a3-f959-5632-b94a-c770e9c6d2a3" :answer/id #uuid "c1fd71a3-f959-5632-b94a-c770e9c6d2a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-78edd9c5-7539-5d54-8eb1-437fb325e3d3" :answer-field/id #uuid "78edd9c5-7539-5d54-8eb1-437fb325e3d3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-3326bfbc-602b-5b97-a232-910eb4540d34" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3326bfbc-602b-5b97-a232-910eb4540d34"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3326bfbc-602b-5b97-a232-910eb4540d34" :answer/id #uuid "3326bfbc-602b-5b97-a232-910eb4540d34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097117 :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-9,5)$ and passes through the point $(7,1).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola with vertex at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),\n$$\n\nand substituting $(h,k)=(-9,5)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(y-5)^{2}=4p(x+9).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(7,1),$ we substitute $x=7$ and $y=1$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1-5)^{2} & =4p(7+9) \\\\ 16 & =4p(16) \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-5)^{2} & =(x+9).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-5)^{2} & =(0+9) \\\\ (y-5)^{2} & =9 \\\\ y-5 & =\\pm 3 \\\\ y & =5\\pm 3 \\\\ y & =2,8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts are $2$\nand $8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186094675 :answer-field/correct 17592186094679 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-4260057c-f969-5185-9095-04c56e87e760" :question/id #uuid "4260057c-f969-5185-9095-04c56e87e760" :question/math-academy-id "q-251823" :question/problem "![](images/15/1500cb3f15e5a32229c861a7b5dcc19e06de0cd6757c8a872f5eb14ad6cb32de.png)\n\n**From top to bottom**, the **exact** values of the $y$-intercepts of the parabola shown above are{{field-1}}\nand \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-1,4)$ and passes through the point $(3,0).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola with vertex at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),\n$$\n\nand substituting $(h,k)=(-1,4)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(y-4)^{2}=4p(x+1).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(3,0),$ we substitute $x=3$ and $y=0$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-4)^{2} & =4p(3+1) \\\\ 16 & =4p(4) \\\\ p & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =4(x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =4(0+1) \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =4 \\\\ y-4 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2+4 \\\\ y & =2,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from top to bottom, the $y$-intercepts are $6$ and  $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-da43aee3-09a1-5940-8ad9-f3914ca15293" "answer-field-816b594c-0ba8-5f8d-b781-18f390478cc1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-da43aee3-09a1-5940-8ad9-f3914ca15293" :answer-field/id #uuid "da43aee3-09a1-5940-8ad9-f3914ca15293" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-199f0fce-6ad5-5b52-bb36-a5c2e347b81d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-199f0fce-6ad5-5b52-bb36-a5c2e347b81d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-199f0fce-6ad5-5b52-bb36-a5c2e347b81d" :answer/id #uuid "199f0fce-6ad5-5b52-bb36-a5c2e347b81d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-816b594c-0ba8-5f8d-b781-18f390478cc1" :answer-field/id #uuid "816b594c-0ba8-5f8d-b781-18f390478cc1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-862218b9-e397-5b8f-8db7-eedde7bba86f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-862218b9-e397-5b8f-8db7-eedde7bba86f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-862218b9-e397-5b8f-8db7-eedde7bba86f" :answer/id #uuid "862218b9-e397-5b8f-8db7-eedde7bba86f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-baa62b58-d974-5e44-ba9b-341e234529fa" :question/id #uuid "baa62b58-d974-5e44-ba9b-341e234529fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-73837" :question/problem "![](images/19/19895cff608c6c9fce2598b235b5415ac2856ccf508f11df52545672918ad6f7.png)\n\nWhat is the $y$-intercept of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-2,-5)$ and passes through the point $(1,4).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nand substituting $(h,k)=(-2,-5)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(x+2)^{2}=4p(y+5).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(1,4),$ we substitute $x=1$ and $y=4$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1+2)^{2} & =4p(4+5) \\\\ 9 & =4p(9) \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2)^{2} & =y+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0+2)^{2} & =y+5 \\\\ 4 & =y+5 \\\\ y & =4-5 \\\\ y & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9132e75d-f34a-5018-bfed-a7561864c4ae"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9132e75d-f34a-5018-bfed-a7561864c4ae" :answer-field/id #uuid "9132e75d-f34a-5018-bfed-a7561864c4ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9e728a1e-a0dc-5359-8857-cc5f28c3dca6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9e728a1e-a0dc-5359-8857-cc5f28c3dca6" "answer-c7aaabf2-9b3d-50fb-a39a-20b69f5186a6" "answer-2021e1ee-a186-5932-a314-361aeb983eb5" "answer-bf011f4b-fdf9-543e-b412-3cda9fe4fcd1" "answer-faf3532c-56de-5ea6-8e58-fe9e6cec5cac"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e728a1e-a0dc-5359-8857-cc5f28c3dca6" :answer/id #uuid "9e728a1e-a0dc-5359-8857-cc5f28c3dca6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7aaabf2-9b3d-50fb-a39a-20b69f5186a6" :answer/id #uuid "c7aaabf2-9b3d-50fb-a39a-20b69f5186a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2021e1ee-a186-5932-a314-361aeb983eb5" :answer/id #uuid "2021e1ee-a186-5932-a314-361aeb983eb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf011f4b-fdf9-543e-b412-3cda9fe4fcd1" :answer/id #uuid "bf011f4b-fdf9-543e-b412-3cda9fe4fcd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-faf3532c-56de-5ea6-8e58-fe9e6cec5cac" :answer/id #uuid "faf3532c-56de-5ea6-8e58-fe9e6cec5cac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097868 :tutorial/content "Let's consider the parabola $(x-1)^2 = \\dfrac 1 2 (y+3) ,$ shown below.\n\n![](images/bb/bbe360c9580cab435e5b737c80c5381f039d1871250cdae3c16bc686e3d0a53d.png)\n\n  \n\nTo calculate the $y$-intercept of the parabola (shown as the point $A$ in the diagram), we set $x=0$ and solve for $y.$ In our case, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(y+3) \\\\ (0-1)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(y+3) \\\\ (-1)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(y+3) \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{1}{2}(y+3) \\\\ 2 & =y+3 \\\\ y & =2-3 \\\\ y & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the coordinates of the $y$-intercept are $(0,-1).$\n\nOn the other hand, to find the $x$-intercepts (shown as the points $B$ and $C$ in the diagram), we set $y=0$ and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(y+3) \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(0+3) \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}} \\\\ x & =1\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the coordinates of $B$ are $\\left(1-\\sqrt{\\dfrac{3}{2}},0\\right)$ and the coordinates of $C$ are $\\left(1+\\sqrt{\\dfrac{3}{2}},0\\right).$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096904 :activity/expected-seconds 720.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
